# Final Project Report

## Overview
This final project used machine learning to build a simple AI DJ recommendation system.

## Dataset
The project used the Music Info.csv file from the Million Song Dataset + Spotify + Last.fm dataset on Kaggle.

## Goal
The goal was to predict whether a user would like a song based on music features such as energy, danceability, valence, tempo, and loudness.

## Models Tested
- Logistic Regression
- Decision Tree
- Random Forest
- K-Nearest Neighbors

## Results
Random Forest and Decision Tree performed the best. Random Forest was selected as the final model because it is usually more stable than a single decision tree.

## What I Learned
I learned how to clean a music dataset, create a simulated target column, train multiple models, compare results, and generate song recommendations.

## Future Improvements
This project could be improved by using real user listening data such as likes, skips, playlist saves, and replay history.
